<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman–Seleucid War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">192–188 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Roman–Seleucid War was fought from 192 to 188 BCE between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a>, with its allies <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pergamon">Pergamon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a>, and the Seleucid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III the Great</a>. Antiochus landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> but was defeated at Thermopylae in 191 BCE and then in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> at Magnesia in 190 BCE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-apamea">Treaty of Apamea</a> (188 BCE) forced him to give up his lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus Mountains</a> and pay a heavy indemnity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-seleucid-war.jpg" alt="Roman–Seleucid War" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: en:William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asia_Minor_188_BCE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
